<Panels>
  <config><![CDATA[{
  "game_id": 73,
  "created_at": "2026-05-21T01:58:40.000Z",
  "level_num": "custom",
  "user_id": 1,
  "properties": {
    "panels": [
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-document-structure-8091c109-8154-48bf-ad2f-1826d0478abb",
        "text": "Every webpage you see has a basic structure, like a blueprint for a house! It all starts with `<!DOCTYPE html>` and the main `<html>` tag.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/9876215638b9bc03b391f68253b86a48-test-lesson-document-structure-panel-1-38e1c22e-41d9-41ac-a9ea-f8fa5d2b7158.png",
        "layout": "text-top-left"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-document-structure-29ae3eac-2f06-4a31-bb6e-5cda9fd04393",
        "text": "Inside the `<html>` tag, we first have the `<head>` section. This is like the hidden foundation or attic of your house; it holds important information *about* the page, but not what you directly see.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/5c097bf4528bd395f60ee9cd0b47cbe3-test-lesson-document-structure-panel-2-e583a7b3-64ca-4979-9989-fa06b924f18e.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-center"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-document-structure-90a6b710-43eb-423b-9da3-e72856339851",
        "text": "Next comes the `<body>` section! This is the main part of your webpage, like the visible rooms of a house. All the content you want users to see goes in here: headings, paragraphs, images, and links.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/920b62b2ebcbdb68babbae172c8224ea-test-lesson-document-structure-panel-3-cce1eecf-8447-4a45-8170-0b8d8a5ab023.png",
        "layout": "text-top-right"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-document-structure-11af1569-cb90-4dc3-bfd2-886e6732b6d7",
        "text": "It's super important to *nest* your HTML tags correctly! Think of it like putting furniture inside rooms, and rooms inside a house. Everything needs to be neatly organized within its parent tag.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/2c0d6de133cefbe98b43410f7d72fbd0-test-lesson-document-structure-panel-4-f0cf2d0f-2b08-463d-9b0d-2452db6703e2.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-left"
      }
    ],
    "generate_outline": "Explain the essential HTML document structure including `<!DOCTYPE html>`, `<html>`, `<head>`, and `<body>` tags. Emphasize the importance of nesting and how elements are organized within each other."
  },
  "published": true,
